00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:41.000
From writing emails to reading CAT scans, millions of people across a wide range of professions now use AI tools to help them do their jobs. In many cases, these tools save time and make us more productive. But as workers increasingly rely on AI tools for critical job tasks, some psychologists are asking, what will happen to our own skills as we hand over more work to artificial intelligence? People have worried about losing skills to technology before. We have GPS, so we rarely bother to look at maps anymore. Calculators change the way we do math. And in aviation, experts have long studied how autopilot affects pilot's skills.
